<section id="basement"><h2>Basement storage: finished, with a secondary office inside</h2>
<p>The 31′7″ × 18′11″ unfinished storage / utility room becomes three zones without boxing in any mechanicals: a <b>secondary office</b> in the middle of the room along the outside wall (the glass desk and Aeron, printer stand, bookcase, cabinet and chest), a <b>storage zone</b> for the gray steel shelving from the garage, the bikes and bins, and a <b>mechanical zone</b> at the family-room end (furnace / air handler, water heater, well pressure tank, softener and brine tank) that stays open with clear service space in front of every unit. The office is a room within the room, like the office in the garage gym, built from freestanding furniture instead of new walls.</p>
<div class="fig2"><figure><a href="img/bs-office.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><img loading="lazy" src="img/bs-office.jpg" alt="Secondary office in basement storage, glass desk behind a wardrobe wall"></a><figcaption>Secondary office: glass desk and Aeron facing the window, framed by a wardrobe wall and an open shelf divider (concept)</figcaption></figure><figure><a href="img/bs-storage.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><img loading="lazy" src="img/bs-storage.jpg" alt="Basement storage zone with shelving and a curtain screening the mechanical area"></a><figcaption>Storage zone and the curtain-screened mechanical area (concept)</figcaption></figure></div>
