<li><b>Walls:</b> drywall the framed perimeter walls in the office and storage zones (insulated, painted warm white). Leave the walls behind the mechanicals open or covered with screwed-on removable panels.</li>
<li><b>Ceiling:</b> paint the open joists, ducts and pipes one color instead of drywalling them, so every valve, cleanout, junction box and duct stays reachable and the room still looks finished.</li>
<li><b>Floor:</b> keep the rubber tiles; add a large rug in the office.</li>
<li><b>Light:</b> existing fixtures, plus a floor lamp and a desk lamp in the office.</li>
</ul></div>
<div class="card"><h3>Freestanding walls, IKEA-style</h3><ul>
<li><b>Office back wall:</b> a run of <a href="https://www.ikea.com/us/en/cat/pax-system-19086/">PAX wardrobes</a> facing the storage side, with the backs finished in slat panels toward the office.</li>
